* ==============================================================================
* Filename: src/main/resources/setup.mqsc
* Purpose: Idempotent MQSC definitions for health-check queues, channels, and security.
* Sensitive-Data Handling: None. No credentials or active client IPs are hardcoded.
* ==============================================================================

* 1. Define Health Check Test Queue
* Set MAXDEPTH appropriately and descriptive text.
DEFINE QLOCAL('DEV.QUEUE.1') +
       DESCR('Core Health Check and Keepalive probe queue') +
       MAXDEPTH(5000) +
       MAXMSGL(4194304) +
       REPLACE

* 2. Define Server Connection Channel with Heartbeat Interval (60 seconds)
* HBINT(60) ensures broken client sockets are cleaned up within 60s of inactivity.
DEFINE CHANNEL('APP.SVRCONN') CHLTYPE(SVRCONN) +
       DESCR('Secure Channel for Application Client Health Probes') +
       HBINT(60) +
       SSLCAUTH(REQUIRED) +
       SSLCIPH('TLS_RSA_WITH_AES_128_CBC_SHA256') +
       REPLACE

* 3. CHLAUTH Mapping Rules (Security Hardening)
* Block all users on APP.SVRCONN by default, then selectively allow health monitor user.
SET CHLAUTH('APP.SVRCONN') TYPE(ADDRESSMAP) ADDRESS('*') USERSRC(MAP) MCAUSER('nobody') WARN(NO) ACTION(REPLACE)

* Map the health check monitor service's specific host IP (e.g., 10.120.45.10) to the designated non-privileged MCA User
SET CHLAUTH('APP.SVRCONN') TYPE(ADDRESSMAP) ADDRESS('10.120.45.10') USERSRC(MAP) MCAUSER('mq_app_user') ACTION(REPLACE)

* 4. Connection Authentication (CONNAUTH) Setup
* Ensure user ID authentication is active and matching credentials.
ALTER QMGR CONNAUTH('SYSTEM.DEFAULT.AUTHINFO.IDPWOS')
REFRESH QMGR TYPE(CONFIG)

* 5. Designated setmqaut commands (To be run by mqm administrator on CLI):
* setmqaut -m QM1 -t qmgr -p mq_app_user +connect +inq
* setmqaut -m QM1 -n DEV.QUEUE.1 -t queue -p mq_app_user +inq +browse +put +get
* setmqaut -m QM1 -n SYSTEM.DEAD.LETTER.QUEUE -t queue -p mq_app_user +inq
